WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.470
- At a virtual court hearing

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.290
for alleged US Capitol rioter,

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:04.560
Anthony Antonio,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.620
his lawyer argued that he
committed those acts because

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.710
of Foxitis or Fox mania.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.530
Because the guy lost his job

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.390
and believed everything that
he was watching on Fox News.

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.920
and that's why he committed
the crime of rioting.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.030
In answer to your questions,

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.180
no Fox News is not going
to face any repercussions

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.389
as a result of this even if
these allegations are true.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.090
Because remember,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.200
people are responsible

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.550
for their own actions.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.690
Love or hate Fox News,

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.730
they don't make people do anything.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.480
I would love to tell you
more about this court hearing

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.470
but it was interrupted

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.720
by fellow alleged US Capitol rioter

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.570
Landon Copeland who heard these words,

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:39.880
was incensed and just
went on a complete rage,

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:40.750
interrupted everything.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:41.583
So in the future,

00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:43.810
we're gonna be seeing a
lot of these guys in court.

